# C and C++. Format: name ## path globs ## regex (ERE) ## why
json-default-accessor ## *.cpp *.h ## \.value\("[A-Za-z_]+", (std::string\(\)|0|false)\) ## a defaulted typed accessor throws on a wrong-typed field in some JSON libraries: is the type checked first, and is a wrong type an error?
json-typed-get ## *.cpp *.h ## \.get<(int|int64_t|uint64_t|std::size_t|std::string)>\(\) ## a typed get on data from outside: is the type checked, the range checked, and an unsigned value above the signed maximum handled?
fixed-temp-name ## *.cpp *.h ## temp_directory_path\(\) / "[^"]*" ## a fixed name under the temp directory: two parallel jobs collide, add a unique suffix
std-regex ## *.cpp *.h ## std::regex[ (]|regex_replace|regex_search ## std::regex on a hot path or on input from outside: slow and can recurse deeply
rename-over-existing ## *.cpp *.h ## (fs|filesystem)::rename\( ## rename does not replace an existing file on every platform: use one replace helper
os-handle-open ## *.cpp *.h ## CreateFileW?\(|CreateProcessW?\(|CreatePipe\(|OpenProcess\(|socket\( ## is the result checked before use, closed on every path, and not inherited by a child that should not have it?
thread-local-pointer ## *.cpp *.h ## thread_local [^=;]*\* ## a thread_local pointer to a caller's object can dangle
strict-serialise ## *.cpp *.h ## \.dump\( ## serialising text that may be invalid UTF-8 throws in some libraries: inside code that must finish a run, replace invalid bytes first
wrong-type-becomes-default ## *.cpp *.h ## \.is_(string|number_integer|number_unsigned|number|boolean|object|array)\(\)[[:space:]]*\?.*:[[:space:]]*(std::string\(\)|""|0|false|nullptr|json::object\(\)|json::array\(\)) ## a type check used as "otherwise the default": a present value of the wrong type is silently treated as absent, where it should be an error
ignored-write-result ## *.cpp *.h ## ^[[:space:]]*(Write|Save|Store|Persist|Remove|Delete|Rename|Replace|Flush|Commit)[A-Za-z_]*\(.*\);[[:space:]]*$ ## the result of a write-like call is dropped: what does the caller report if it failed, and is anything deleted afterwards on the assumption that it worked?
loop-over-client-member ## *.cpp *.h ## for[[:space:]]*\((const )?auto[&]*[[:space:]]+[A-Za-z_]+[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*[A-Za-z_]+(\[|\.at\() ## a loop over a member of JSON from a client or a file: bounded (count and size) before the work, or only after the whole array was copied or parsed?
